Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: comctl32: Enlarge the standard toolbar bitmaps for the DPI.
 The standard images (IDB_STD_*, IDB_VIEW_*, IDB_HIST_*) are 16 or 24
 pixels at any DPI. Enlarge them by a whole factor, the DPI scale rounded
 to the nearest whole number, with pixel replication. Images that the
 application adds to the same toolbar are fitted into the larger cells,
 and TB_SETBITMAPSIZE with the 16 or 24 pixel size of the standard images
 is taken as a request for their size at the DPI.
 .
 Windows leaves this to the application, which asks TB_GETBITMAPFLAGS and
 loads large images itself. Doing it here covers the Open and Save
 dialogs and WordPad without changing each caller; the size test in
 TB_SETBITMAPSIZE is a heuristic for that.
 .
 TB_GETBITMAPFLAGS asked a NULL DC for the DPI and never reported
 TBBF_LARGE; it uses the system DPI.
Last-Modified: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:50:00 +0300

